Having the same issue. The hashes from `main-app` and `webpack` are created by Webpack, it doesn't look like they are using the buildId (not sure if this was possible in the past).

One thing that I tried is to tweak the webpack config in the `next.config.js`:

```js
const config = {
  webpack: (config, options) => {
    const { dev } = options;
    if (!dev) {
      const hash = process.env.GIT_COMMIT_SHA || 'static-id';
      config.output = {
        ...config.output,
        filename: `[name].${hash}.js`,
      };
    }
    return config;
  },
};
```

